================================================================================
   MACHINE LEGITIMATION, SANCTIONS, REDRESS (ARTICLE 12)
================================================================================
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | PROHIBITION OF MACHINE LEGITIMATION                        |
   |   A bare assertion that "society desires X" or "data       |
   |   establishes Y" carries no legal weight.                  |
   |   No decision may rest SOLELY on a machine-asserted        |
   |   premise; the human-authored reasoning must be stated.    |
   |   Empirical evidence, AI-generated analysis and            |
   |   predictive modelling remain admissible INPUTS to human   |
   |   deliberation.                                            |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | NULLITY OF FULL RIGHT                                      |
   |   Any act, consultation, rule-making or procurement        |
   |   without a prior, compliant, published audit is VOID AB   |
   |   INITIO, subject to the RELIANCE RULE below.              |
   |   STANDING: natural and legal persons, CSOs,               |
   |   parliamentary minority >= 10%, affected individuals.     |
   |   Missing or deficient audit -> interlocutory injunction   |
   |   halting automated processing, option generation and      |
   |   administrative implementation. Where a halt would        |
   |   itself endanger life or critical services, the court     |
   |   orders safe state or degraded mode instead.              |
   |   MATERIALITY:                                             |
   |     - missing ENTIRE deliverable = strict nullity          |
   |     - missing one of >= 3 rejected framings without a      |
   |       reasoned record = nullity                            |
   |     - minor formal defect with no impact on                |
   |       contestability = cure with notice                    |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | RELIANCE RULE (applies to Article 12 AND Article 14)       |
   |   Good-faith third-party acts are not automatically void.  |
   |   The court may modulate temporal effects, preserve the    |
   |   act where voiding would be disproportionate, or order    |
   |   compensation from the responsible agency.                |
   |   Benefits already paid are not clawed back from           |
   |   recipients acting in good faith.                         |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | UNIFIED PENALTY SCHEDULE (Art 12, Art 14, IRA Level 4)     |
   |   Tier 1 first minor breach:                               |
   |     reprimand + mandatory retraining.                      |
   |   Tier 2 material or repeated breach:                      |
   |     withholding of up to 5% of the SPECIFIC AI operations  |
   |     budget line.                                           |
   |   Tier 3 knowing breach or repeat within 24 months:        |
   |     up to 10% of that line, plus suspension or removal of  |
   |     the responsible official.                              |
   |   HARD CAP: 10% of the AI operations line.                 |
   |   Never statutory services; never a general levy on        |
   |   taxpayers. Liability graded by severity of harm,         |
   |   knowledge and repetition.                                |
   |   Safety-critical operations are exempt from withholding;  |
   |   the sanction applies to the agency discretionary AI      |
   |   budget instead.                                          |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | INDIVIDUAL REDRESS (Full Cycle AND Emergency decisions)    |
   |   The agency must give NOTICE of the decision and of the   |
   |   redress rights; the 90-day clock runs from notice.       |
   |   Claim for:                                               |
   |     (a) re-examination by an uninvolved human              |
   |         decision-maker;                                    |
   |     (b) compensation for material harm caused by a         |
   |         defective audit or by an emergency later found     |
   |         unjustified.                                       |
   |   Redress is independent of the nullity action and         |
   |   survives cure.                                           |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+


