================================================================================
   PERIODIC EVALUATION - COGNITIVE SOVEREIGNTY FACTORS
================================================================================
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Evaluated every 2-3 years by independent assessment.       |
   | All rates are PER DECISION (decisions in scope in the      |
   | period), never per affected person.                        |
   | Bands are INITIAL VALUES set for the first cycle.          |
   | The IRA must publish a RECALIBRATION METHODOLOGY within    |
   | 12 months, using at least two of:                          |
   |   (a) observed distributions across pilot jurisdictions,   |
   |   (b) a structured expert Delphi process,                  |
   |   (c) comparison with analogous governance metrics such    |
   |       as audit failure rates or ombudsman complaint rates. |
   | Until that methodology is published, the initial bands     |
   | below govern.                                              |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | R_refus        = share of Full-Cycle proposals rejected or |
   |                  amended by the mini-public                |
   |                  Band 5-20%. Sustained 0% signals capture. |
   | A_alternatives = mean rejected framings per audit          |
   |                  Band >= 3, including >= 1 dissenting.     |
   | C_contestation = share of decisions subject to a           |
   |                  successful challenge                       |
   |                  Band 2-15%. Near 0 = no access; high =    |
   |                  excessive litigation.                     |
   | T_traceability = Registry completeness score,              |
   |                  independently audited                     |
   |                  Band >= 95%.                              |
   | P_plurality    = effective number of distinct objective-   |
   |                  function families                          |
   |                  Band 3-7. High may indicate fragmentation.|
   | E_economy      = MODIFIER, not a sixth factor              |
   |                  audit cost per decision as % of the       |
   |                  decision's procurement budget             |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | SCORING RUBRIC (0-4 per factor)                            |
   |   4 = inside band                                          |
   |   3 = within 10% of the band edge                          |
   |   2 = within 25% of the band edge                          |
   |   1 = within 50% of the band edge                          |
   |   0 = beyond 50%                                           |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+
   | AGGREGATION RULE                                           |
   |   The five factors are NOT multiplied. Each factor is      |
   |   scored 0-4 against its band. The five scores are summed  |
   |   (range 0-20).                                            |
   |   E_economy applies as a modifier:                         |
   |     > 15% : total reduced by 1 point                       |
   |     > 30% : total reduced by 2 points                      |
   |   A total < 10 triggers a mandatory reform proposal to     |
   |   Parliament within 6 months.                              |
   +------------------------------------------------------------+


